14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 63,4 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 6,9, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 5,9 a 8,0. En diciembre se adjudicó el 14 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 14 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 282 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.904 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no implica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a factores como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No se puede inferir actos ilícitos solo por la cantidad de contratos cerca del límite.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con periodos de alta demanda o presupuestos cerrados.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 436 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 63.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.9 to 8.0. December accounts for 14% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 14% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 20. Contract [1], for 14,904 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove any contract was improperly awarded. Prices near the limit can reflect market rates or budget constraints. Legitimate reasons may explain why contracts are just under the limit.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts awarded in December. Look at how many contracts go to the same awardee. Review if multiple contracts cover the same need to ensure no overlap or duplication.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["w8MVPOdlhmHL1rX3q%2FMAPA%3D%3D","PnOsjcHkg5pSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","V0sQDkGvo24Xhk1FZxEyvw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}